From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:47:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: arm extra wake sources from a
 runtime list

The tree arms T8140's six wake sources on T8132: the PMU's alarm
(NUB.SPMI0.SW3), the first USB port (ATC0.USBWakeup), the SMC and the
MTP. The J604's ADT lists 25 ap-wake-sources and macOS leaves all of
them unmasked; the J604's other two USB-C ports (ATC1, ATC3), the CIO
wakes, the NUB timer and GPIO and the AOP's sources stay masked here,
so a USB device plugged into either right-hand port can't wake it.

Which of them hold up through a deep sleep on Linux isn't known: one
whose block isn't kept up may wake the SoC at once. Add
apple_sleep.wake_extra=, a list of source numbers armed on top of the
tree's for each sleep, so that one kernel can try them one at a time.
Empty by default: nothing changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
index 317e2f750e..8bb0580931 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
@@ -1827,6 +1827,17 @@ static void sleep_wake_unmask(const struct apple_sleep *s, u32 *val, u32 id)
  * source 0 is masked with the rest: that held under macOS with its handler hidden,
  * as did leaving it enabled with the AMCC enables off. The two together are unmeasured.
  */
+/*
+ * Sources armed on top of the tree's apple,wake-enable, by number, for this boot's sleeps. The
+ * tree arms T8140's six; the ADT lists 25 and macOS leaves all of them unmasked. One whose
+ * block isn't kept up for the sleep may wake it at once: that is what a try with it shows.
+ */
+static int wake_extra[8];
+static int wake_extra_count;
+module_param_array(wake_extra, int, &wake_extra_count, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(wake_extra,
+		 "Wake sources armed on top of the device tree's, by number (default none)");
+
 static void sleep_wake_masks(struct apple_sleep *s, u32 *val)
 {
 	int i;
@@ -1835,6 +1846,9 @@ static void sleep_wake_masks(struct apple_sleep *s, u32 *val)
 		val[i] = i == s->soc->wake_words - 1 ? s->soc->wake_last_word : U32_MAX;
 	for (i = 0; i < s->wake_enable_count; i++)
 		sleep_wake_unmask(s, val, s->wake_enable[i]);
+	for (i = 0; i < READ_ONCE(wake_extra_count) && i < ARRAY_SIZE(wake_extra); i++)
+		if (wake_extra[i] >= 0)
+			sleep_wake_unmask(s, val, wake_extra[i]);
 }
 
 /* The last checks, then the stray words lowered: what has stopped may not return until a wake. */
-- 
